*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/quizsprint/fly.toml
app = "quizoi-management"
primary_region = "iad"

[build]
  dockerfile = "Dockerfile"

[env]
  NODE_ENV = "production"
  PORT = "8080"

[http_service]
  internal_port = 8080
  force_https = true
  auto_stop_machines = "stop"
  auto_start_machines = true
  min_machines_running = 0
  processes = ["app"]

  [http_service.concurrency]
    type = "requests"
    soft_limit = 25
    hard_limit = 50

  [[http_service.checks]]
    interval = "15s"
    timeout = "3s"
    grace_period = "20s"
    method = "GET"
    path = "/api/health"

[[vm]]
  memory = "512mb"
  cpu_kind = "shared"
  cpus = 1
*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/quizsprint/FLY_DEPLOYMENT.md
# Deploy Quizio on Fly.io

## 1. Commit the Container Files

Commit `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, `fly.toml`, the server change, package scripts, and this guide to the repository connected to Fly. Fly then detects the Dockerfile and builds the project as a Node container rather than trying to guess the Expo runtime.

## 2. Required Fly Secrets

Set the following **Secrets** in the Fly dashboard. Do not place these values in `fly.toml`, Git, or browser-visible build arguments.

| Fly secret | Required | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Yes | Production MySQL connection string used by Quizio’s server and content dashboard. |
| `JWT_SECRET` | Yes | Long random secret used to sign and verify administrator sessions. Use at least 32 random characters. |
| `OAUTH_SERVER_URL` | Yes for current login implementation | Server URL used to exchange OAuth codes and validate sign-in sessions. |
| `BUILT_IN_FORGE_API_URL` | Only if using Manus-hosted storage URLs | Enables the optional `/manus-storage/*` proxy. |
| `BUILT_IN_FORGE_API_KEY` | Only if using Manus-hosted storage URLs | Secret key for that optional storage proxy. |

## 3. Required Fly Build Arguments

Expo places these values into the browser bundle at image-build time. They are not secrets, but use the real production values. Add them in Fly’s **Build Arguments** or pass them in your deployment command.

| Build argument | Required | Example / role |
|---|---:|---|
| `VITE_APP_ID` | Yes for current OAuth | The OAuth application/project identifier. |
| `VITE_OAUTH_PORTAL_URL` | Yes for current OAuth | The browser sign-in portal URL. |
| `OAUTH_SERVER_URL` | Yes for current OAuth | Same public OAuth server URL used by the backend. |
| `OWNER_OPEN_ID` | Yes | Your OAuth user identifier. This account becomes the Quizio administrator. |
| `OWNER_NAME` | Recommended | Administrator display name. |
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` | Leave empty for same-origin Fly hosting | Set only if the API is hosted on a different HTTPS domain. |

Because the current dashboard uses a Manus-oriented OAuth flow, the OAuth provider must allow this Fly callback URL before browser sign-in can work:

```text
https://quizoi-management.fly.dev/api/oauth/callback
```

If you migrate the dashboard authentication to Supabase Auth, replace the OAuth values with your Supabase URL and server-side service credentials instead. Do not expose a Supabase service-role key to the browser bundle.

## 4. Database Preparation

The existing data layer expects **MySQL**, not PostgreSQL. Use a managed MySQL service that allows Fly connections, set its SSL parameters in `DATABASE_URL` if required, then run the Drizzle migrations once from a trusted environment:

```bash
pnpm drizzle-kit generate
pnpm drizzle-kit migrate
```

The dashboard will not work until the `users`, `quiz_categories`, `quiz_questions`, and `quiz_imports` tables exist. The health endpoint only confirms that the server is alive; it does not prove database credentials are correct.

## 5. Deploy and Verify

After adding the secrets and build arguments, deploy through Fly. Verify these URLs:

| URL | Expected result |
|---|---|
| `https://quizoi-management.fly.dev/api/health` | JSON with `ok: true`. |
| `https://quizoi-management.fly.dev/admin` | Private dashboard sign-in gate. |
| `https://quizoi-management.fly.dev/` | Quizio web player. |

Use a single Fly hostname for the player, dashboard, and API. This keeps the administrator session cookie same-origin and avoids cross-domain cookie configuration.

## Production Note

The app’s Android player must use a reachable HTTPS API base URL to download remote questions. For a Fly deployment, set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://quizoi-management.fly.dev` when generating a new Android build if the app does not use the same web origin.
